#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma mengenai maklumat dan pengiraan kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stabilizer codes"
msgstr "Kod penstabil"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore notin */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore notin */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll define stabilizer codes in general.\n"
"We'll also discuss some of their basic properties and how they work, including how states can be encoded and how errors are detected and corrected using these codes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan takrifkan kod penstabil secara umum.\n"
"Kita juga akan bincangkan beberapa sifat asasnya dan cara ia berfungsi, termasuk bagaimana keadaan boleh dikodkan dan bagaimana ralat dikesan serta dibetulkan menggunakan kod-kod ini.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Definition of stabilizer codes {#definition-of-stabilizer-codes}"
msgstr "Takrifan kod penstabil {#definition-of-stabilizer-codes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An $n$-qubit stabilizer code is specified by a list of $n$-qubit Pauli operations, $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"These operations are called *stabilizer generators* in this context, and they must satisfy the following three properties.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod penstabil $n$-qubit ditentukan oleh senarai operasi Pauli $n$-qubit, $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Operasi-operasi ini dipanggil *penjana penstabil* dalam konteks ini, dan ia mesti memenuhi tiga sifat berikut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The stabilizer generators all *commute* with one another.\n"
msgstr "Semua penjana penstabil *kalis tukar tertib* antara satu sama lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_j P_k = P_k P_j \\qquad \\text{(for all $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_j P_k = P_k P_j \\qquad \\text{(untuk semua $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The stabilizer generators form a *minimal generating set*.\n"
msgstr "Penjana penstabil membentuk *set penjana minimum*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_{k-1},P_{k+1},\\ldots,P_r\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(for all $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_{k-1},P_{k+1},\\ldots,P_r\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(untuk semua $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At least one quantum state vector is fixed by all of the stabilizer "
"generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekurang-kurangnya satu vektor keadaan kuantum ditetapkan oleh semua penjana"
" penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   -\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   -\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   (It's not obvious that the existence of a quantum state vector "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ fixed by all of the stabilizer generators, meaning "
"$P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = "
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ is equivalent to $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} \\notin "
"\\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle,$ but indeed this is the case, and we'll "
"see why a bit later in the lesson.)\n"
msgstr ""
"   (Ia tidak jelas bahawa kewujudan vektor keadaan kuantum "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang ditetapkan oleh semua penjana penstabil, "
"bermaksud $P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = "
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ adalah setara dengan $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} "
"\\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle,$ tetapi memang begitulah, dan "
"kita akan lihat sebabnya sedikit kemudian dalam pelajaran ini.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that we have such a list $P_1,\\ldots,P_r,$ the *code space* "
"defined by these stabilizer generators is the subspace $\\mathcal{C}$ "
"containing every $n$-qubit quantum state vector fixed by all $r$ of these "
"stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengandaikan kita mempunyai senarai $P_1,\\ldots,P_r$ seperti itu, "
"*ruang kod* yang ditakrifkan oleh penjana penstabil ini ialah subruang "
"$\\mathcal{C}$ yang mengandungi setiap vektor keadaan kuantum $n$-qubit yang"
" ditetapkan oleh kesemua $r$ penjana penstabil ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{C} = \\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\,:\\, P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{C} = \\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\,:\\, P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum state vectors in this subspace are precisely the ones that can be viewed as *valid encodings* of quantum states.\n"
"We'll discuss the actual process of encoding later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Vektor keadaan kuantum dalam subruang ini adalah tepat vektor yang boleh dilihat sebagai *pengekodan sah* bagi keadaan kuantum.\n"
"Kita akan bincangkan proses pengekodan sebenar kemudian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, the *stabilizer* of the code defined by the stabilizer generators "
"$P_1, \\ldots, P_r$ is the set generated by these operations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, *penstabil* bagi kod yang ditakrifkan oleh penjana penstabil $P_1,"
" \\ldots, P_r$ ialah set yang dijana oleh operasi-operasi ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural way to think about a stabilizer code is to view the stabilizer generators as observables, and to collectively interpret the outcomes of the measurements associated with these observables as an error syndrome.\n"
"Valid encodings are $n$-qubit quantum state vectors for which the measurement outcomes, as eigenvalues, are all guaranteed to be $+1.$\n"
"Any other syndrome, where at least one $-1$ measurement outcome occurs, signals that an error has been detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara semula jadi untuk memahami kod penstabil ialah dengan melihat penjana penstabil sebagai boleh pemerhatian, dan mentafsirkan secara kolektif hasil ukuran yang berkaitan dengan boleh pemerhatian ini sebagai sindrom ralat.\n"
"Pengekodan sah ialah vektor keadaan kuantum $n$-qubit di mana hasil ukuran, sebagai nilai eigen, semua dijamin bernilai $+1.$\n"
"Sebarang sindrom lain, di mana sekurang-kurangnya satu hasil ukuran $-1$ berlaku, memberi isyarat bahawa ralat telah dikesan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at several examples shortly, but first just a few remarks "
"about the three conditions on stabilizer generators are in order.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan lihat beberapa contoh tidak lama lagi, tetapi dahulu ada beberapa "
"catatan mengenai tiga syarat pada penjana penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first condition is natural, in light of the interpretation of the stabilizer generators as observables, for it implies that it doesn't matter in what order the measurements are performed: the observables commute, so the measurements commute.\n"
"This naturally imposes certain algebraic constraints on stabilizer codes that are important to how they work.\n"
msgstr ""
"Syarat pertama adalah semula jadi, mengambil kira tafsiran penjana penstabil sebagai boleh pemerhatian, kerana ia membayangkan bahawa tidak kira dalam urutan mana ukuran dilakukan: boleh pemerhatian kalis tukar tertib, jadi ukuran pun kalis tukar tertib.\n"
"Ini secara semula jadi mengenakan kekangan algebra tertentu pada kod penstabil yang penting kepada cara ia berfungsi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second condition requires that the stabilizer generators form a minimal generating set, meaning that removing any one of them would result in a smaller stabilizer.\n"
"Strictly speaking, this condition isn't really essential to the way stabilizer codes work in an *operational* sense — and, as we'll see in the next lesson, it does sometimes make sense to think about sets of stabilizer generators for codes that actually don't satisfy this condition.\n"
"For the sake of *analyzing* stabilizer codes and explaining their properties, however, we will assume that this condition is in place.\n"
"In short, this condition guarantees that each observable that we measure to obtain the error syndrome *adds* information about possible errors, as opposed to being redundant and producing results that could be inferred from the other stabilizer generator measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Syarat kedua memerlukan penjana penstabil membentuk set penjana minimum, bermaksud mengeluarkan mana-mana satu daripadanya akan menghasilkan penstabil yang lebih kecil.\n"
"Secara ketatnya, syarat ini sebenarnya tidak penting kepada cara kod penstabil berfungsi dalam *erti kata operasi* — dan, seperti yang akan kita lihat dalam pelajaran seterusnya, ada kalanya masuk akal untuk memikirkan set penjana penstabil bagi kod yang sebenarnya tidak memenuhi syarat ini.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, untuk tujuan *menganalisis* kod penstabil dan menerangkan sifatnya, kita akan mengandaikan syarat ini wujud.\n"
"Ringkasnya, syarat ini memastikan setiap boleh pemerhatian yang kita ukur untuk mendapatkan sindrom ralat *menambah* maklumat tentang kemungkinan ralat, dan bukannya berlebihan serta menghasilkan keputusan yang boleh disimpulkan daripada ukuran penjana penstabil lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The third condition requires that at least one nonzero vector is fixed by all of the stabilizer generators, which is equivalent to $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ not being contained in the stabilizer.\n"
"The need for this condition comes from the fact that it actually is possible to choose a minimal generating set of $n$-qubit Pauli operations that all commute with one another, and yet no nonzero vectors are fixed by every one of the operations.\n"
"We're not interested in \"codes\" for which there are no valid encodings, so we rule out this possibility by requiring this condition as a part of the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Syarat ketiga memerlukan sekurang-kurangnya satu vektor bukan sifar ditetapkan oleh semua penjana penstabil, yang bersamaan dengan $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ tidak terkandung dalam penstabil.\n"
"Keperluan syarat ini timbul daripada hakikat bahawa sebenarnya mungkin untuk memilih set penjana minimum operasi Pauli $n$-qubit yang semuanya kalis tukar tertib antara satu sama lain, namun tiada vektor bukan sifar yang ditetapkan oleh setiap operasi tersebut.\n"
"Kita tidak berminat dengan \"kod\" yang tiada pengekodan sah, jadi kita menolak kemungkinan ini dengan mewajibkan syarat ini sebagai sebahagian daripada takrifan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr "Contoh-contoh {#examples}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are some examples of stabilizer codes for small values of $n.$\n"
"We'll see more examples, including ones for which $n$ can be much larger, in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah beberapa contoh kod penstabil untuk nilai $n$ yang kecil.\n"
"Kita akan lihat lebih banyak contoh, termasuk yang mana $n$ boleh menjadi lebih besar, dalam pelajaran seterusnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3-bit repetition code {#3-bit-repetition-code}"
msgstr "Kod ulangan 3-bit {#3-bit-repetition-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 3-bit repetition code is an example of a stabilizer code, where our stabilizer generators are\n"
"$Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod ulangan 3-bit adalah contoh kod penstabil, di mana penjana penstabil kita ialah\n"
"$Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ dan $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can easily check that these two stabilizer generators fulfill the required conditions.\n"
"First, the two stabilizer generators $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z$ commute with one another.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh semak dengan mudah bahawa kedua-dua penjana penstabil ini memenuhi syarat yang diperlukan.\n"
"Pertama, kedua-dua penjana penstabil $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ dan $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z$ kalis tukar tertib antara satu sama lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z) = Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\n"
"= (\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z)(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z) = Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\n"
"= (\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z)(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, we have a minimal generating set (rather trivially in this case).\n"
msgstr "Kedua, kita mempunyai set penjana minimum (agak mudah dalam kes ini).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\notin \\langle\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\notin \\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\notin \\langle\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\notin \\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And third, we already know that $\\vert 000\\rangle$ and $\\vert 111\\rangle,$ as well as any linear combination of these vectors, are fixed by both $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"
"Alternatively, we can conclude this using the equivalent condition from the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dan ketiga, kita sudah tahu bahawa $\\vert 000\\rangle$ dan $\\vert 111\\rangle,$ serta sebarang gabungan linear vektor-vektor ini, ditetapkan oleh kedua-dua $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ dan $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"
"Sebagai alternatif, kita boleh menyimpulkan ini menggunakan syarat setara daripada takrifan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"-\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\notin\n"
"\\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"= \\{\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z,\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\n"
"\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"-\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\notin\n"
"\\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"= \\{\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z,\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\n"
"\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These conditions can be much more difficult to check for more complicated "
"stabilizer codes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Syarat-syarat ini boleh menjadi jauh lebih sukar untuk disemak bagi kod "
"penstabil yang lebih rumit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Modified 3-bit repetition code {#modified-3-bit-repetition-code}"
msgstr "Kod ulangan 3-bit yang diubahsuai {#modified-3-bit-repetition-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson, we saw that it's possible to modify the 3-bit repetition code so that it protects against phase-flip errors rather than bit-flip errors.\n"
"As a stabilizer code, this new code is easy to describe:\n"
"its stabilizer generators are $X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes X.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran sebelumnya, kita melihat bahawa adalah mungkin untuk mengubah suai kod ulangan 3-bit supaya ia melindungi terhadap ralat pembalikan fasa dan bukannya ralat pembalikan bit.\n"
"Sebagai kod penstabil, kod baru ini mudah diterangkan:\n"
"penjana penstabilnya ialah $X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ dan $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes X.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This time the stabilizer generators represent $X\\otimes X$ observables rather than $Z\\otimes Z$ observables, so they're essentially parity checks in the plus/minus basis rather than the standard basis.\n"
"The three required conditions on the stabilizer generators are easily verified, along similar lines to the ordinary 3-bit repetition code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kali ini penjana penstabil mewakili boleh pemerhatian $X\\otimes X$ dan bukannya boleh pemerhatian $Z\\otimes Z$, jadi pada dasarnya ia adalah semakan pariti dalam asas tambah/tolak dan bukannya asas piawai.\n"
"Tiga syarat yang diperlukan pada penjana penstabil mudah disahkan, mengikut garis yang sama seperti kod ulangan 3-bit biasa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "9-qubit Shor code {#9-qubit-shor-code}"
msgstr "Kod Shor 9-qubit {#9-qubit-shor-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the 9-qubit Shor code, which is also a stabilizer code, expressed by "
"stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah kod Shor 9-qubit, yang juga merupakan kod penstabil, "
"dinyatakan dengan penjana penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case, we basically have three copies of the 3-bit repetition code, one for each of the three blocks of three qubits,\n"
"as well as the last two stabilizer generators, which take a form reminiscent of the circuit for detecting phase flips for this code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kes ini, kita pada dasarnya mempunyai tiga salinan kod ulangan 3-bit, satu untuk setiap tiga blok tiga qubit,\n"
"serta dua penjana penstabil terakhir, yang mengambil bentuk yang mengingatkan kita kepada litar untuk mengesan pembalikan fasa bagi kod ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative way to think about the last two stabilizer generators is that"
" they take the same form as for the 3-bit repetition code for phase flips, "
"except that $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ is substituted for $X,$ which is "
"consistent with the fact that $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ corresponds to an $X$ "
"operation on logical qubits encoded using the 3-bit repetition code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara alternatif untuk memahami dua penjana penstabil terakhir ialah bahawa "
"mereka mengambil bentuk yang sama seperti kod ulangan 3-bit untuk pembalikan"
" fasa, kecuali $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ digantikan dengan $X,$ yang konsisten"
" dengan hakikat bahawa $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ berpadanan dengan operasi $X$"
" pada qubit logik yang dikodkan menggunakan kod ulangan 3-bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we move on to other examples, it should be noted that tensor product symbols are often omitted when describing stabilizer codes by lists of stabilizer generators, because it tends to make them easier to read and to see their patterns.\n"
"For example, the same stabilizer generators as above for the 9-qubit Shor code look like this without the tensor product symbols being written explicitly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum kita beralih ke contoh lain, perlu diperhatikan bahawa simbol hasil darab tensor sering ditinggalkan apabila menerangkan kod penstabil dengan senarai penjana penstabil, kerana ia cenderung memudahkan pembacaan dan penglihatan polanya.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, penjana penstabil yang sama seperti di atas untuk kod Shor 9-qubit kelihatan seperti ini tanpa simbol hasil darab tensor ditulis secara eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}&\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}&\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "7-qubit Steane code {#7-qubit-steane-code}"
msgstr "Kod Steane 7-qubit {#7-qubit-steane-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's another example of a stabilizer code, known as the *7-qubit Steane code*.\n"
"It has some remarkable features, and we'll come back to this code from time to time throughout the remaining lessons of the course.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh lain kod penstabil, yang dikenali sebagai *kod Steane 7-qubit*.\n"
"Ia mempunyai beberapa ciri yang luar biasa, dan kita akan kembali kepada kod ini dari semasa ke semasa sepanjang pelajaran-pelajaran selebihnya dalam kursus ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & X & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & X & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For now, let's simply observe that this is a valid stabilizer code.\n"
"The first three stabilizer generators clearly commute with one another, because $Z$ commutes with itself and the identity commutes with everything, and the situation is similar for the last three stabilizer generators.\n"
"It remains to check that if we take one of the $Z$-stabilizer generators (that is, one of the first three) and one of the $X$-stabilizer generators (that is, one of the last three), then these two generators commute, and one can go through the 9 possible pairings to check that.\n"
"In all of these cases, an $X$ and a $Z$ Pauli matrix always line up in the same position an even number of times, so the two generators will commute, just like $X\\otimes X$ and $Z\\otimes Z$ commute.\n"
"This is also a minimal generating set, and it defines a nontrivial code space, which are facts left to you to contemplate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Buat masa ini, mari kita perhatikan sahaja bahawa ini adalah kod penstabil yang sah.\n"
"Tiga penjana penstabil pertama jelas kalis tukar tertib antara satu sama lain, kerana $Z$ kalis tukar tertib dengan dirinya sendiri dan identiti kalis tukar tertib dengan segalanya, dan situasi serupa bagi tiga penjana penstabil terakhir.\n"
"Yang tinggal ialah menyemak bahawa jika kita ambil satu penjana $Z$ (iaitu salah satu daripada tiga yang pertama) dan satu penjana $X$ (iaitu salah satu daripada tiga yang terakhir), maka kedua-dua penjana ini kalis tukar tertib, dan seseorang boleh melalui 9 kemungkinan pasangan untuk menyemaknya.\n"
"Dalam semua kes ini, matriks Pauli $X$ dan $Z$ sentiasa berjajar pada kedudukan yang sama dengan bilangan genap, jadi kedua-dua penjana akan kalis tukar tertib, sama seperti $X\\otimes X$ dan $Z\\otimes Z$ kalis tukar tertib.\n"
"Ini juga merupakan set penjana minimum, dan ia menakrifkan ruang kod yang tidak trivial, yang merupakan fakta-fakta yang diserahkan kepada anda untuk direnungkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 7-qubit Steane code is similar to the 9-qubit Shor code in that it "
"encodes a single qubit and allows for the correction of an arbitrary error "
"on one qubit, but it requires only 7 qubits rather than 9.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod Steane 7-qubit menyerupai kod Shor 9-qubit kerana ia mengekodkan satu "
"qubit dan membolehkan pembetulan ralat sewenang-wenangnya pada satu qubit, "
"tetapi hanya memerlukan 7 qubit dan bukannya 9.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5-qubit code {#5-qubit-code}"
msgstr "Kod 5-qubit {#5-qubit-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Seven is not the fewest number of qubits required to encode one qubit and "
"protect it against an arbitrary error on one qubit — here's a stabilizer "
"code that does this using just 5 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tujuh bukanlah bilangan qubit paling sedikit yang diperlukan untuk "
"mengekodkan satu qubit dan melindunginya daripada ralat sewenang-wenangnya "
"pada satu qubit — berikut adalah kod penstabil yang melakukan ini "
"menggunakan hanya 5 qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccc}\n"
"X & Z & Z & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z & X \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccc}\n"
"X & Z & Z & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z & X \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This code is typically called *the 5-qubit code.*\n"
"This is the smallest number of qubits in a quantum error correcting code that can allow for the correction of an arbitrary single-qubit error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod ini biasanya dipanggil *kod 5-qubit.*\n"
"Ini adalah bilangan qubit minimum dalam kod pembetulan ralat kuantum yang boleh membolehkan pembetulan ralat sewenang-wenangnya pada satu qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "One-dimensional stabilizer codes {#one-dimensional-stabilizer-codes}"
msgstr "Kod penstabil satu dimensi {#one-dimensional-stabilizer-codes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's another example of a stabilizer code, though it doesn't actually encode any qubits:\n"
"the code space is one-dimensional.\n"
"It is, however, still a valid stabilizer code by the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh lain kod penstabil, walaupun sebenarnya ia tidak mengekodkan sebarang qubit:\n"
"ruang kodnya berdimensi satu.\n"
"Namun demikian, ia masih merupakan kod penstabil yang sah mengikut takrifan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specifically, the code space is the one-dimensional space spanned by an "
"e-bit $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Khususnya, ruang kod ialah ruang satu dimensi yang direntangi oleh e-bit "
"$\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a related example of a stabilizer code whose code space is the one-"
"dimensional space spanned by a GHZ state $(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert "
"111\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh berkaitan kod penstabil yang ruang kodnya ialah ruang "
"satu dimensi yang direntangi oleh keadaan GHZ $(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert "
"111\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Code space dimension {#code-space-dimension}"
msgstr "Dimensi ruang kod {#code-space-dimension}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a stabilizer code, described by $n$-qubit stabilizer generators $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Perhaps the very first question that comes to mind about this code is, \"How many qubits does it encode?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan kita mempunyai kod penstabil, yang diterangkan oleh penjana penstabil $n$-qubit $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Mungkin soalan pertama yang terlintas di fikiran mengenai kod ini ialah, \"Berapa banyak qubit yang dikodkannya?\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This question has a simple answer.\n"
"Assuming that the $n$-qubit stabilizer generators $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$ satisfy the three requirements of the definition (namely, that the stabilizer generators all commute with one another, that this is a minimal generating set, and that the code space is nonempty), it must then be that the code space for this stabilizer code has dimension $2^{n-r},$ so $n-r$ qubits can be encoded using this code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Soalan ini mempunyai jawapan yang mudah.\n"
"Dengan mengandaikan bahawa penjana penstabil $n$-qubit $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$ memenuhi tiga keperluan takrifan (iaitu, penjana penstabil semuanya kalis tukar tertib antara satu sama lain, ini adalah set penjana minimum, dan ruang kod tidak kosong), maka ruang kod bagi kod penstabil ini mesti berdimensi $2^{n-r},$ jadi $n-r$ qubit boleh dikodkan menggunakan kod ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, we have $n$ qubits to use for this encoding, and each stabilizer generator effectively \"takes a qubit away\" in terms of how many qubits we can encode.\n"
"Note that this is not about which or how many *errors* can be detected or corrected, it is only a statement about the dimension of the code space.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara intuitif, kita mempunyai $n$ qubit untuk digunakan dalam pengekodan ini, dan setiap penjana penstabil secara berkesan \"mengambil satu qubit\" dari segi berapa banyak qubit yang boleh kita kodkan.\n"
"Perlu diingat bahawa ini bukan tentang ralat mana atau berapa banyak yang boleh dikesan atau dibetulkan, ia hanyalah pernyataan tentang dimensi ruang kod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, for both the 3-bit repetition code and the modified version of that code for phase-flip errors, we have $n=3$ qubits and $r=2$ stabilizer generators, and therefore these codes can each encode 1 qubit.\n"
"For another example, consider the 5-qubit code: we have 5 qubits and 4 stabilizer generators, so once again the code space has dimension 2, meaning that one qubit can be encoded using this code.\n"
"For one final example, the code whose stabilizer generators are $X\\otimes X$ and $Z\\otimes Z$ has a one-dimensional code space, spanned by the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ which is consistent with having $n=2$ qubits and $r=2$ stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, untuk kedua-dua kod ulangan 3-bit dan versi yang diubah suai untuk ralat pembalikan fasa, kita mempunyai $n=3$ qubit dan $r=2$ penjana penstabil, dan oleh itu setiap kod ini boleh mengekodkan 1 qubit.\n"
"Sebagai contoh lain, pertimbangkan kod 5-qubit: kita mempunyai 5 qubit dan 4 penjana penstabil, jadi sekali lagi ruang kod berdimensi 2, bermaksud satu qubit boleh dikodkan menggunakan kod ini.\n"
"Untuk satu contoh terakhir, kod yang penjana penstabilnya ialah $X\\otimes X$ dan $Z\\otimes Z$ mempunyai ruang kod satu dimensi, yang direntangi oleh keadaan $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ yang konsisten dengan mempunyai $n=2$ qubit dan $r=2$ penjana penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's see how this fact can be proved.\n"
"The first step is to observe that, because the stabilizer generators commute, and because every Pauli operation is its own inverse, every element in the stabilizer can be expressed as a product\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita lihat bagaimana fakta ini boleh dibuktikan.\n"
"Langkah pertama ialah memerhatikan bahawa, kerana penjana penstabil kalis tukar tertib, dan kerana setiap operasi Pauli adalah songsangannya sendiri, setiap elemen dalam penstabil boleh dinyatakan sebagai hasil darab\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_1^{a_1} \\cdots P_r^{a_r},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_1^{a_1} \\cdots P_r^{a_r},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $a_1,\\ldots,a_r\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"Equivalently, each element of the stabilizer is obtained by multiplying together some subset of the stabilizer generators.\n"
"Indeed, every stabilizer element can be expressed *uniquely* in this way, due to the condition that $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\}$ is a minimal generating set.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $a_1,\\ldots,a_r\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"Secara setara, setiap elemen penstabil diperoleh dengan mendarabkan beberapa subset penjana penstabil bersama-sama.\n"
"Sememangnya, setiap elemen penstabil boleh dinyatakan secara *unik* dengan cara ini, disebabkan syarat bahawa $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\}$ adalah set penjana minimum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, define $\\Pi_k$ to be the projection onto the space of $+1$-eigenvectors of $P_k,$ for each $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}.$\n"
"These projections can be obtained by averaging the corresponding Pauli operations with the identity operation as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, takrifkan $\\Pi_k$ sebagai unjuran ke atas ruang vektor eigen $+1$ bagi $P_k,$ untuk setiap $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}.$\n"
"Unjuran-unjuran ini boleh diperoleh dengan mengambil purata operasi Pauli yang berpadanan dengan operasi identiti seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_k = \\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_k}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_k = \\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_k}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code space $\\mathcal{C}$ is the subspace of all vectors that are fixed "
"by all $r$ of the stabilizer generators $P_1,\\ldots,P_r,$ or equivalently, "
"all $r$ of the projections $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ruang kod $\\mathcal{C}$ ialah subruang semua vektor yang ditetapkan oleh "
"kesemua $r$ penjana penstabil $P_1,\\ldots,P_r,$ atau setaranya, kesemua $r$"
" unjuran $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given that the stabilizer generators all commute with one another, the projections $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r$ must also commute.\n"
"This allows us to use a fact from linear algebra, which is that the *product* of these projections is the projection onto the *intersection* of the subspaces corresponding to the individual projections.\n"
"That is to say, the product $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ is the projection onto the code space $\\mathcal{C}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan penjana penstabil semuanya kalis tukar tertib antara satu sama lain, unjuran $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r$ juga mestilah kalis tukar tertib.\n"
"Ini membolehkan kita menggunakan fakta dari algebra linear, iaitu *hasil darab* unjuran-unjuran ini adalah unjuran ke atas *persilangan* subruang yang berpadanan dengan unjuran individu.\n"
"Dengan kata lain, hasil darab $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ adalah unjuran ke atas ruang kod $\\mathcal{C}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now expand out the product $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ using the formulas "
"for these projections to obtain the following expression.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini boleh kembangkan hasil darab $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ menggunakan "
"formula untuk unjuran-unjuran ini untuk mendapatkan ungkapan berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r\n"
"= \\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_1}{2}\\biggr)\\cdots\\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_r}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2^r}\\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r\n"
"= \\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_1}{2}\\biggr)\\cdots\\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_r}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2^r}\\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In words, the projection onto the code space of a stabilizer code is equal, "
"as a matrix, to the *average* over all of the elements in the stabilizer of "
"that code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kata-kata, unjuran ke atas ruang kod bagi kod penstabil adalah sama, "
"sebagai matriks, dengan *purata* ke atas semua elemen dalam penstabil kod "
"tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we can compute the dimension of the code space by using the fact that the dimension of any subspace is equal to the trace of the projection onto that subspace.\n"
"Thus, the dimension of the code space $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by the following formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, kita boleh mengira dimensi ruang kod dengan menggunakan fakta bahawa dimensi mana-mana subruang adalah sama dengan jejak unjuran ke atas subruang tersebut.\n"
"Oleh itu, dimensi ruang kod $\\mathcal{C}$ diberikan oleh formula berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r})\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can evaluate this expression by making use of a couple of basic facts.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh menilai ungkapan ini dengan menggunakan beberapa fakta asas.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We have $P_1^0 \\cdots P_r^0 = \\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ and therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mempunyai $P_1^0 \\cdots P_r^0 = \\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ dan oleh "
"itu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) = 2^n.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) = 2^n.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For $(a_1,\\ldots,a_r) \\neq (0,\\ldots,0),$ the product $P_1^{a_1}\\cdots "
"P_r^{a_r}$ must be $\\pm 1$ times a Pauli operation — but we cannot obtain "
"$\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ because this would contradict the minimality of "
"the set $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\},$ and we cannot obtain "
"$-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ because the third condition on the stabilizer "
"generators forbids it. Therefore, because the trace of every non-identity "
"Pauli operation is zero, we obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk $(a_1,\\ldots,a_r) \\neq (0,\\ldots,0),$ hasil darab $P_1^{a_1}\\cdots"
" P_r^{a_r}$ mestilah $\\pm 1$ kali operasi Pauli — tetapi kita tidak boleh "
"mendapat $\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ kerana ini akan bercanggah dengan "
"keminimuman set $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\},$ dan kita tidak boleh mendapat "
"$-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ kerana syarat ketiga pada penjana penstabil "
"melarangnya. Oleh itu, kerana jejak setiap operasi Pauli bukan identiti "
"adalah sifar, kita mendapat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) = 0.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) = 0.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The dimension of the code space is therefore $2^{n-r}$ as claimed:\n"
msgstr "Dimensi ruang kod oleh itu adalah $2^{n-r}$ seperti yang dituntut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) & =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) \\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2^r} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = 2^{n-r}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) & =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) \\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2^r} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = 2^{n-r}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an aside, we can now see that the assumption that $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ is not contained in the stabilizer implies that the code space must contain at least one quantum state vector.\n"
"This is because, as we've just verified, this assumption implies that the code space has dimension $2^{n-r},$ which cannot be zero.\n"
"The converse implication happens to be trivial: if $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ is contained in the stabilizer, then the code space can't possibly contain any quantum state vectors, because no nonzero vectors are fixed by this operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai catatan, kita kini dapat melihat bahawa andaian bahawa $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ tidak terkandung dalam penstabil membayangkan bahawa ruang kod mesti mengandungi sekurang-kurangnya satu vektor keadaan kuantum.\n"
"Ini kerana, seperti yang baru kita sahkan, andaian ini membayangkan bahawa ruang kod berdimensi $2^{n-r},$ yang tidak boleh sifar.\n"
"Implikasi sebaliknya kebetulan adalah trivial: jika $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ terkandung dalam penstabil, maka ruang kod tidak mungkin mengandungi sebarang vektor keadaan kuantum, kerana tiada vektor bukan sifar yang ditetapkan oleh operasi ini.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clifford operations and encodings {#clifford-operations-and-encodings}"
msgstr "Operasi Clifford dan pengekodan {#clifford-operations-and-encodings}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we'll briefly discuss how qubits can be encoded using stabilizer "
"codes, but to do that we first need to introduce *Clifford operations*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, kita akan membincangkan secara ringkas bagaimana qubit boleh "
"dikodkan menggunakan kod penstabil, tetapi untuk melakukan itu kita perlu "
"memperkenalkan *operasi Clifford* terlebih dahulu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clifford operations {#clifford-operations}"
msgstr "Operasi Clifford {#clifford-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Clifford operations are unitary operations, on any number of qubits, that can be implemented by quantum circuits with a restricted set of gates:\n"
"- Hadamard gates\n"
"- $S$ gates\n"
"- CNOT gates\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi Clifford adalah operasi uniter, pada sebarang bilangan qubit, yang boleh dilaksanakan oleh litar kuantum dengan set get yang terhad:\n"
"- get Hadamard\n"
"- get $S$\n"
"- get CNOT\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that $T$ gates are not included, nor are Toffoli gates and Fredkin gates.\n"
"Not only are those gates not included in the list, but in fact, it's not possible to implement those gates using the ones listed here; they're not Clifford operations.\n"
"Pauli operations, on the other hand, are Clifford operations because they can be implemented with sequences of Hadamard and $S$ gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa get $T$ tidak disertakan, begitu juga get Toffoli dan get Fredkin.\n"
"Bukan sahaja get-get tersebut tidak disertakan dalam senarai, malah tidak mungkin untuk melaksanakan get-get itu menggunakan yang disenaraikan di sini; ia bukan operasi Clifford.\n"
"Operasi Pauli, sebaliknya, adalah operasi Clifford kerana ia boleh dilaksanakan dengan jujukan get Hadamard dan get $S$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That's a simple way to define Clifford operations, but it doesn't explain why they're defined like this or what's special about this particular collection of gates.\n"
"The *real* reason Clifford operations are defined like this is that, up to global phase factors, the Clifford operations are precisely the unitary operations that always transform Pauli operations into Pauli operations by conjugation.\n"
"To be more precise, an $n$-qubit unitary operation $U$ is equivalent to a Clifford operation up to a phase factor if, and only if, for *every* $n$-qubit Pauli operation $P,$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Itulah cara mudah untuk mendefinisikan operasi Clifford, tetapi ia tidak menerangkan mengapa ia didefinisikan seperti ini atau apa yang istimewa tentang koleksi get tertentu ini.\n"
"Sebab *sebenar* operasi Clifford didefinisikan seperti ini adalah kerana, sehingga faktor fasa global, operasi Clifford adalah tepat operasi uniter yang sentiasa mengubah operasi Pauli kepada operasi Pauli melalui konjugasi.\n"
"Untuk lebih tepat, operasi uniter $n$-qubit $U$ adalah setara dengan operasi Clifford sehingga faktor fasa jika, dan hanya jika, untuk *setiap* operasi Pauli $n$-qubit $P,$ kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U P U^{\\dagger} = \\pm Q\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U P U^{\\dagger} = \\pm Q\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some $n$-qubit Pauli operation $Q.$\n"
msgstr "untuk sesetengah operasi Pauli $n$-qubit $Q.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Note that it is not possible to have $U P U^{\\dagger} = \\alpha Q$ for $\\alpha\\notin\\{+1,-1\\}$ when $U$ is unitary and $P$ and $Q$ are Pauli operations.\n"
"This follows from the fact that the matrix on the left-hand side of the equation in question is both unitary and Hermitian, and $+1$ and $-1$ are the only choices for $\\alpha$ that allow the right-hand side to be unitary and Hermitian as well.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Perhatikan bahawa tidak mungkin untuk mempunyai $U P U^{\\dagger} = \\alpha Q$ untuk $\\alpha\\notin\\{+1,-1\\}$ apabila $U$ adalah uniter dan $P$ dan $Q$ adalah operasi Pauli.\n"
"Ini mengikuti dari fakta bahawa matriks di sebelah kiri persamaan tersebut adalah uniter dan Hermitian, dan $+1$ serta $-1$ adalah satu-satunya pilihan untuk $\\alpha$ yang membolehkan sebelah kanan menjadi uniter dan Hermitian juga.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is straightforward to verify the conjugation property just described when $U$ is a Hadamard, $S,$ or CNOT gate.\n"
"In particular, this is easy for Hadamard gates,\n"
msgstr ""
"Adalah mudah untuk mengesahkan sifat konjugasi yang baru diterangkan apabila $U$ adalah get Hadamard, $S,$ atau CNOT.\n"
"Khususnya, ini mudah untuk get Hadamard,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H X H^{\\dagger} = Z, \\qquad\n"
"H Y H^{\\dagger} = -Y, \\qquad\n"
"H Z H^{\\dagger} = X,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H X H^{\\dagger} = Z, \\qquad\n"
"H Y H^{\\dagger} = -Y, \\qquad\n"
"H Z H^{\\dagger} = X,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and $S$ gates,\n"
msgstr "dan get $S$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"S X S^{\\dagger} = Y, \\qquad\n"
"S Y S^{\\dagger} = -X, \\qquad\n"
"S Z S^{\\dagger} = Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"S X S^{\\dagger} = Y, \\qquad\n"
"S Y S^{\\dagger} = -X, \\qquad\n"
"S Z S^{\\dagger} = Z.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For CNOT gates, there are 15 non-identity Pauli operations on two qubits to check.\n"
"Naturally, they can be checked individually — but the relationships between CNOT gates and $X$ and $Z$ gates listed (in circuit form) in the previous lesson, together with the multiplication rules for Pauli matrices, offer a shortcut to the same conclusion.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk get CNOT, terdapat 15 operasi Pauli bukan identiti pada dua qubit yang perlu diperiksa.\n"
"Secara semula jadi, ia boleh diperiksa secara individu — tetapi hubungan antara get CNOT dan get $X$ serta $Z$ yang disenaraikan (dalam bentuk litar) dalam pelajaran sebelumnya, bersama dengan peraturan pendaraban matriks Pauli, menawarkan jalan pintas kepada kesimpulan yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once we know this conjugation property is true for Hadamard, $S,$ and CNOT "
"gates, we can immediately conclude that it is true for *circuits* composed "
"of these gates — which is to say, all Clifford operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah kita tahu sifat konjugasi ini benar untuk get Hadamard, $S,$ dan "
"CNOT, kita boleh segera menyimpulkan bahawa ia benar untuk *litar* yang "
"terdiri daripada get-get ini — iaitu, semua operasi Clifford.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is more difficult to prove that the relationship works in the other direction, which is that if a given unitary operation $U$ satisfies the conjugation property for Pauli operations, then it must be possible to implement it (up to a global phase) using just Hadamard, $S,$ and CNOT gates.\n"
"This won't be explained in this lesson, but it is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih sukar untuk membuktikan bahawa hubungan ini berfungsi dalam arah yang lain, iaitu bahawa jika operasi uniter tertentu $U$ memenuhi sifat konjugasi untuk operasi Pauli, maka ia mestilah mungkin untuk melaksanakannya (sehingga fasa global) menggunakan hanya get Hadamard, $S,$ dan CNOT.\n"
"Ini tidak akan diterangkan dalam pelajaran ini, tetapi ia adalah benar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Clifford operations are not universal for quantum computation; unlike universal sets of quantum gates, approximating arbitrary unitary operations to any desired level of accuracy with Clifford operations is not possible.\n"
"Indeed, for a given value of $n,$ there are only *finitely* many $n$-qubit Clifford operations (up to phase factors).\n"
"Performing Clifford operations on standard basis states followed by standard basis measurements also can't allow us to perform computations that are outside of the reach of classical algorithms — because we can *efficiently simulate* computations of this form classically.\n"
"This fact is known as the *Gottesman-Knill theorem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi Clifford bukan universal untuk pengkomputeran kuantum; tidak seperti set get universal, menghampiri operasi uniter sembarangan kepada sebarang tahap ketepatan dengan operasi Clifford adalah tidak mungkin.\n"
"Malah, untuk nilai tertentu $n,$ hanya terdapat *finit* banyak operasi Clifford $n$-qubit (sehingga faktor fasa).\n"
"Melakukan operasi Clifford pada keadaan asas standard diikuti dengan pengukuran asas standard juga tidak boleh membenarkan kita melakukan pengiraan yang berada di luar jangkauan algoritma klasik — kerana kita boleh *mensimulasikan dengan cekap* pengiraan dalam bentuk ini secara klasik.\n"
"Fakta ini dikenali sebagai *teorem Gottesman-Knill*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encoders for stabilizer codes {#encoders-for-stabilizer-codes}"
msgstr "Pengekod untuk kod penstabil {#encoders-for-stabilizer-codes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A stabilizer code defines a code space of a certain dimension, and we have the freedom to use that code space however we choose —\n"
"nothing forces us to encode qubits into this code space in a specific way.\n"
"It is always possible, however, to use a *Clifford operation* as an encoder, if we choose to do that.\n"
"To be more precise, for any stabilizer code that allows $m$ qubits to be encoded into $n$ qubits, there's an $n$-qubit Clifford operation $U$ such that, for any $m$-qubit quantum state vector $\\vert\\phi\\rangle,$ we have that\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod penstabil mentakrifkan ruang kod berdimensi tertentu, dan kita mempunyai kebebasan untuk menggunakan ruang kod itu sebagaimana yang kita mahu —\n"
"tiada apa yang memaksa kita untuk mengkodkan qubit ke dalam ruang kod ini dengan cara yang khusus.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, sentiasa mungkin untuk menggunakan *operasi Clifford* sebagai pengekod, jika kita memilih untuk berbuat demikian.\n"
"Untuk lebih tepat, untuk sebarang kod penstabil yang membolehkan $m$ qubit dikodkan ke dalam $n$ qubit, terdapat operasi Clifford $n$-qubit $U$ supaya, untuk sebarang vektor keadaan kuantum $m$-qubit $\\vert\\phi\\rangle,$ kita ada bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = U \\bigl(\\vert 0^{n-m} \\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = U \\bigl(\\vert 0^{n-m} \\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a quantum state vector in the code space of our code that we may "
"interpret as an encoding of $\\vert\\phi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"adalah vektor keadaan kuantum dalam ruang kod kita yang boleh kita tafsirkan"
" sebagai pengekodan $\\vert\\phi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is good because Clifford operations are relatively simple, compared with arbitrary unitary operations, and there are ways to optimize their implementation using techniques similar to ones found in the proof of the Gottesman-Knill theorem.\n"
"As a result, circuits for encoding states using stabilizer codes never need to be too large.\n"
"In particular, it is always possible to perform an encoding for an $n$-qubit stabilizer code using a Clifford operation that requires $O(n^2/\\log(n))$ gates.\n"
"This is because *every* Clifford operation on $n$ qubits can be implemented by a circuit of this size.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah baik kerana operasi Clifford adalah relatif mudah, berbanding dengan operasi uniter sembarangan, dan terdapat cara untuk mengoptimumkan pelaksanaannya menggunakan teknik yang serupa dengan yang ditemui dalam bukti teorem Gottesman-Knill.\n"
"Akibatnya, litar untuk mengkodkan keadaan menggunakan kod penstabil tidak perlu terlalu besar.\n"
"Khususnya, sentiasa mungkin untuk melakukan pengekodan bagi kod penstabil $n$-qubit menggunakan operasi Clifford yang memerlukan $O(n^2/\\log(n))$ get.\n"
"Ini kerana *setiap* operasi Clifford pada $n$ qubit boleh dilaksanakan oleh litar bersaiz ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, here's an encoder for the 7-qubit Steane code.\n"
"It is indeed a Clifford operation, and as it turns out, this one doesn't even need $S$ gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, berikut adalah pengekod untuk kod Steane 7-qubit.\n"
"Ia memang merupakan operasi Clifford, dan ternyata, yang ini tidak memerlukan get $S$ pun.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Clifford encoder for the 7-qubit Steane "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/Steane-encoder.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pengekod Clifford untuk kod Steane "
"7-qubit](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/Steane-encoder.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Detecting errors {#detecting-errors}"
msgstr "Mengesan ralat {#detecting-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an $n$-qubit stabilizer code described by stabilizer generators "
"$P_1,\\ldots, P_r,$ error detection works in the following way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kod penstabil $n$-qubit yang diterangkan oleh penjana penstabil "
"$P_1,\\ldots, P_r,$ pengesanan ralat berfungsi dengan cara berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To detect errors, all of the stabilizer generators are measured as observables.\n"
"There are $r$ stabilizer generators, and therefore $r$ measurement outcomes, each one being $+1$ or $-1$ (or a binary value if we choose to associate $0$ with $+1$ and $1$ with $-1,$ respectively).\n"
"We interpret the $r$ outcomes collectively, as a vector or string, as a *syndrome.*\n"
"The syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1)$ indicates that no error has been detected, while at least one $-1$ somewhere within the syndrome indicates an error has been detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengesan ralat, semua penjana penstabil diukur sebagai boleh pemerhatian.\n"
"Terdapat $r$ penjana penstabil, dan oleh itu $r$ hasil pengukuran, setiap satu adalah $+1$ atau $-1$ (atau nilai binari jika kita memilih untuk mengaitkan $0$ dengan $+1$ dan $1$ dengan $-1,$ masing-masing).\n"
"Kita mentafsirkan $r$ hasil secara kolektif, sebagai vektor atau rentetan, sebagai *sindrom.*\n"
"Sindrom $(+1,\\ldots,+1)$ menunjukkan bahawa tiada ralat telah dikesan, manakala sekurang-kurangnya satu $-1$ di mana-mana dalam sindrom menunjukkan bahawa ralat telah dikesan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose, in particular, that $E$ is an $n$-qubit Pauli operation, representing a hypothetical error.\n"
"(We're only considering Pauli operations as errors, by the way, because the discretization of errors works the same way for arbitrary stabilizer codes as it does for the 9-qubit Shor code.)\n"
"There are three cases that determine whether or not $E$ is detected as an error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan, khususnya, bahawa $E$ adalah operasi Pauli $n$-qubit, mewakili ralat hipotetikal.\n"
"(Kita hanya mempertimbangkan operasi Pauli sebagai ralat, dengan cara, kerana pendiskretan ralat berfungsi dengan cara yang sama untuk kod penstabil sembarangan seperti untuk kod Shor 9-qubit.)\n"
"Terdapat tiga kes yang menentukan sama ada $E$ dikesan sebagai ralat atau tidak.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Error detection cases {#error-detection-cases}"
msgstr "Kes-kes pengesanan ralat {#error-detection-cases}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The operation $E$ is proportional to an element in the stabilizer.\n"
msgstr "Operasi $E$ adalah berkadar dengan elemen dalam penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   E = \\pm Q \\; \\text{for some}\\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   E = \\pm Q \\; \\text{untuk sesetengah}\\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case, $E$ must commute with every stabilizer generator, so we "
"obtain the syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$  This means that $E$ is not detected "
"as an error.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kes ini, $E$ mestilah kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap penjana "
"penstabil, jadi kita memperoleh sindrom $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$  Ini bermakna $E$"
" tidak dikesan sebagai ralat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $E$ is not proportional to an element in the stabilizer, but "
"it nevertheless commutes with every stabilizer generator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi $E$ tidak berkadar dengan elemen dalam penstabil, tetapi ia tetap "
"kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap penjana penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   E\\neq \\pm Q\\; \\text{for} \\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle, \\;\\text{but}\\;\n"
"   E P_k = P_k E \\;\\text{for every}\\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   E\\neq \\pm Q\\; \\text{untuk} \\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle, \\;\\text{tetapi}\\;\n"
"   E P_k = P_k E \\;\\text{untuk setiap}\\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This is an error that changes vectors in the code space in some "
"nontrivial way. But, because $E$ commutes with every stabilizer generator, "
"the syndrome is $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ so $E$ goes undetected by the code.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ini adalah ralat yang mengubah vektor dalam ruang kod dengan cara yang "
"tidak trivial. Tetapi, kerana $E$ kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap penjana "
"penstabil, sindromnya adalah $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ jadi $E$ tidak dikesan oleh "
"kod.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $E$ anti-commutes with at least one of the stabilizer "
"generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi $E$ anti-kalis-tukar-tertib dengan sekurang-kurangnya satu daripada "
"penjana penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k E = -E P_k \\; \\text{for at least one} \\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k E = -E P_k \\; \\text{untuk sekurang-kurangnya satu} \\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The syndrome is different than $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ so the error $E$ is "
"detected by the code.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Sindromnya berbeza daripada $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ jadi ralat $E$ dikesan "
"oleh kod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the first case, the error $E$ is not a concern because this operation "
"does nothing to vectors in the code space, except to possibly inject an "
"irrelevant global phase: $E \\ket{\\psi} = \\pm\\ket{\\psi}$ for every "
"encoded state $\\ket{\\psi}.$ In essence, this is not actually an error — "
"whatever nontrivial action $E$ may have happens outside of the code space — "
"so it's good that $E$ is not detected as an error, because nothing needs to "
"be done about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kes pertama, ralat $E$ bukan kebimbangan kerana operasi ini tidak "
"melakukan apa-apa pada vektor dalam ruang kod, kecuali mungkin menyuntik "
"fasa global yang tidak relevan: $E \\ket{\\psi} = \\pm\\ket{\\psi}$ untuk "
"setiap keadaan terkod $\\ket{\\psi}.$ Pada dasarnya, ini bukan sebenarnya "
"ralat — apa jua tindakan tidak trivial yang mungkin dilakukan oleh $E$ "
"berlaku di luar ruang kod — jadi adalah baik bahawa $E$ tidak dikesan "
"sebagai ralat, kerana tiada apa yang perlu dilakukan mengenainya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second case, intuitively speaking, is the bad case.\n"
"It's the *anti-commutation* of an error with a stabilizer generator that causes a $-1$ to appear somewhere in the syndrome, signaling an error, but that doesn't happen in this case.\n"
"So, we have an error $E$ that does change vectors in the code space in some nontrivial way, but it goes undetected by the code.\n"
"For example, for the 3-bit repetition code, the operation $E = X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ falls into this category.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kes kedua, secara intuitif, adalah kes yang buruk.\n"
"Ia adalah *anti-kalis-tukar-tertib* bagi ralat dengan penjana penstabil yang menyebabkan $-1$ muncul di mana-mana dalam sindrom, menandakan ralat, tetapi itu tidak berlaku dalam kes ini.\n"
"Jadi, kita mempunyai ralat $E$ yang memang mengubah vektor dalam ruang kod dengan cara yang tidak trivial, tetapi ia tidak dikesan oleh kod.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, untuk kod repetisi 3-bit, operasi $E = X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ termasuk dalam kategori ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact that such an error $E$ must change some vectors in the code space in a non-trivial way can be argued as follows.\n"
"By the assumption that $E$ commutes with $P_1,\\ldots,P_r$ but is not proportional to a stabilizer element, we can conclude that we would obtain a new, valid stabilizer code by including $E$ as a stabilizer generator along with $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"The code space for this new code, however, has only half the dimension of the original code space, from which we can conclude that the action of $E$ on the original code space cannot be proportional to the identity operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fakta bahawa ralat $E$ sedemikian mestilah mengubah beberapa vektor dalam ruang kod dengan cara yang tidak trivial boleh dihujahkan seperti berikut.\n"
"Dengan andaian bahawa $E$ kalis tukar tertib dengan $P_1,\\ldots,P_r$ tetapi tidak berkadar dengan elemen penstabil, kita boleh menyimpulkan bahawa kita akan mendapat kod penstabil yang baru dan sah dengan memasukkan $E$ sebagai penjana penstabil bersama-sama dengan $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Ruang kod untuk kod baru ini, bagaimanapun, hanya mempunyai separuh dimensi daripada ruang kod asal, dari mana kita boleh menyimpulkan bahawa tindakan $E$ pada ruang kod asal tidak boleh berkadar dengan operasi identiti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the last of the three cases, which is that the error $E$ anti-commutes with at least one stabilizer generator,\n"
"the syndrome has at least one $-1$ somewhere in it, which indicates that something is wrong.\n"
"As we have already discussed, the syndrome won't uniquely identify $E$ in general, so it's still necessary to choose a correction operation for each syndrome, which might or might not correct the error $E.$\n"
"We'll discuss this step shortly, in the last part of the lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kes terakhir daripada tiga kes, iaitu ralat $E$ anti-kalis-tukar-tertib dengan sekurang-kurangnya satu penjana penstabil,\n"
"sindromnya mempunyai sekurang-kurangnya satu $-1$ di dalamnya, yang menunjukkan bahawa ada sesuatu yang tidak kena.\n"
"Seperti yang telah kita bincangkan, sindrom tidak akan mengenal pasti $E$ secara unik secara umum, jadi masih perlu memilih operasi pembetulan untuk setiap sindrom, yang mungkin atau mungkin tidak membetulkan ralat $E.$\n"
"Kita akan membincangkan langkah ini tidak lama lagi, dalam bahagian terakhir pelajaran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Distance of a stabilizer code {#distance-of-a-stabilizer-code}"
msgstr "Jarak kod penstabil {#distance-of-a-stabilizer-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a point of terminology, when we refer to the *distance* of a stabilizer code, we mean the *minimum weight* of a Pauli operation $E$ that falls into the second category above — meaning that it changes the code space in some nontrivial way, but the code doesn't detect this.\n"
"When it is said that a stabilizer code is an $[[n,m,d]]$ stabilizer code, using double square brackets, this means the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai terminologi, apabila kita merujuk kepada *jarak* kod penstabil, kita bermaksud *berat minimum* operasi Pauli $E$ yang termasuk dalam kategori kedua di atas — bermakna ia mengubah ruang kod dengan cara yang tidak trivial, tetapi kod tidak mengesannya.\n"
"Apabila dikatakan bahawa kod penstabil adalah kod penstabil $[[n,m,d]]$, menggunakan kurungan segi empat sama berganda, ini bermakna yang berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encodings are $n$ qubits in length,\n"
msgstr "Pengekodan adalah $n$ qubit panjangnya,\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "the code allows for the encoding $m$ qubits, and\n"
msgstr "kod membolehkan pengekodan $m$ qubit, dan\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "the distance of the code is $d.$\n"
msgstr "jarak kod adalah $d.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an example, let's consider the 7-qubit Steane code.\n"
"Here are the stabilizer generators for this code:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, mari kita pertimbangkan kod Steane 7-qubit.\n"
"Berikut adalah penjana penstabil untuk kod ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This code has distance 3, and we can argue this as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod ini mempunyai jarak 3, dan kita boleh menghujahkan ini seperti "
"berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First consider any Pauli operation $E$ having weight at most 2, and suppose this operation commutes with all six stabilizer generators.\n"
"We will conclude that $E$ must be the identity operation, which (as always) is an element of the stabilizer.\n"
"This will show that the distance of the code is strictly greater than 2.\n"
"Suppose, in particular, that $E$ takes the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama pertimbangkan sebarang operasi Pauli $E$ yang mempunyai berat paling banyak 2, dan andaikan operasi ini kalis tukar tertib dengan semua enam penjana penstabil.\n"
"Kita akan menyimpulkan bahawa $E$ mestilah operasi identiti, yang (seperti biasa) adalah elemen penstabil.\n"
"Ini akan menunjukkan bahawa jarak kod adalah lebih besar daripada 2.\n"
"Andaikan, khususnya, bahawa $E$ mengambil bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"E = P \\otimes Q \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"E = P \\otimes Q \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $P$ and $Q$ being possibly non-identity Pauli matrices.\n"
"This is just one case, and it is necessary to repeat the argument that follows for all of the other possible locations for non-identity Pauli matrices among the tensor factors of $E,$ but the argument is essentially the same for all of the possible locations.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk $P$ dan $Q$ sebagai matriks Pauli yang mungkin bukan identiti.\n"
"Ini hanyalah satu kes, dan perlu mengulangi hujah yang mengikuti untuk semua lokasi lain yang mungkin untuk matriks Pauli bukan identiti antara faktor tensor $E,$ tetapi hujahnya pada dasarnya sama untuk semua lokasi yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $E$ commutes with all six stabilizer generators, so it "
"commutes with these two in particular:\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi $E$ kalis tukar tertib dengan semua enam penjana penstabil, jadi ia "
"kalis tukar tertib dengan dua ini khususnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The tensor factor $Q$ in our error $E$ lines up with the identity matrix in both of these stabilizer generators (which is why they were selected).\n"
"Given that we have identity matrices in the rightmost 5 positions of $E,$ we conclude that $P$ must commute with $X$ and $Z,$ for otherwise $E$ would anti-commute with one of the two generators.\n"
"However, the only Pauli matrix that commutes with both $X$ and $Z$ is the identity matrix, so $P = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Faktor tensor $Q$ dalam ralat $E$ kita sejajar dengan matriks identiti dalam kedua-dua penjana penstabil ini (itulah sebabnya ia dipilih).\n"
"Memandangkan kita mempunyai matriks identiti dalam 5 kedudukan paling kanan $E,$ kita menyimpulkan bahawa $P$ mestilah kalis tukar tertib dengan $X$ dan $Z,$ kerana jika tidak $E$ akan anti-kalis-tukar-tertib dengan salah satu daripada dua penjana.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, satu-satunya matriks Pauli yang kalis tukar tertib dengan kedua-dua $X$ dan $Z$ adalah matriks identiti, jadi $P = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we know this, we can choose two more stabilizer generators that have an $X$ and a $Z$ in the second position from left, and we draw a similar conclusion: $Q = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"It is therefore the case that $E$ is the identity operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang setelah kita tahu ini, kita boleh memilih dua lagi penjana penstabil yang mempunyai $X$ dan $Z$ dalam kedudukan kedua dari kiri, dan kita membuat kesimpulan yang serupa: $Q = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"Oleh itu, $E$ adalah operasi identiti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, there's no way for an error having weight at most 2 to go undetected by this code, unless the error is the identity operation (which is in the stabilizer and therefore not actually an error).\n"
"On the other hand, there are weight 3 Pauli operations that commute with all six of these stabilizer generators, but aren't proportional to stabilizer elements, such as $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X\\otimes X\\otimes X$\n"
"and $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\\otimes Z.$\n"
"This establishes that this code has distance 3, as claimed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, tidak ada cara bagi ralat yang mempunyai berat paling banyak 2 untuk tidak dikesan oleh kod ini, kecuali ralat itu adalah operasi identiti (yang ada dalam penstabil dan oleh itu bukan sebenarnya ralat).\n"
"Sebaliknya, terdapat operasi Pauli berat 3 yang kalis tukar tertib dengan semua enam penjana penstabil ini, tetapi tidak berkadar dengan elemen penstabil, seperti $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X\\otimes X\\otimes X$\n"
"dan $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\\otimes Z.$\n"
"Ini menetapkan bahawa kod ini mempunyai jarak 3, seperti yang diklaim.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correcting errors {#correcting-errors}"
msgstr "Membetulkan ralat {#correcting-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last topic of discussion for this lesson is the *correction* of errors for stabilizer codes.\n"
"As usual, assume that we have a stabilizer code specified by n-qubit stabilizer generators $P_1, \\ldots, P_r.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Topik perbincangan terakhir untuk pelajaran ini adalah *pembetulan* ralat untuk kod penstabil.\n"
"Seperti biasa, andaikan kita mempunyai kod penstabil yang dinyatakan oleh penjana penstabil $n$-qubit $P_1, \\ldots, P_r.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $n$-qubit Pauli operations, as errors that could affect states encoded using this code, are partitioned into equal-sized collections according to which syndrome they cause to appear.\n"
"There are $2^r$ distinct syndromes and $4^n$ Pauli operations, which means there are $4^n/2^r$ Pauli operations causing each syndrome.\n"
"Any one of these errors could be responsible for the corresponding syndrome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi Pauli $n$-qubit, sebagai ralat yang boleh mempengaruhi keadaan yang dikodkan menggunakan kod ini, dibahagikan kepada koleksi bersaiz sama mengikut sindrom yang ia hasilkan.\n"
"Terdapat $2^r$ sindrom yang berbeza dan $4^n$ operasi Pauli, yang bermaksud terdapat $4^n/2^r$ operasi Pauli yang menyebabkan setiap sindrom.\n"
"Mana-mana satu daripada ralat ini boleh bertanggungjawab untuk sindrom yang bersesuaian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, among the $4^n/2^r$ Pauli operations that cause each syndrome, there are some that should be considered as being equivalent.\n"
"In particular, if the product of two Pauli operations is proportional to a stabilizer element, then those two operations are effectively equivalent as errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, antara $4^n/2^r$ operasi Pauli yang menyebabkan setiap sindrom, terdapat beberapa yang patut dianggap setara.\n"
"Khususnya, jika hasil darab dua operasi Pauli adalah berkadar dengan elemen penstabil, maka kedua-dua operasi tersebut secara berkesan setara sebagai ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another way to say this is that if we apply a correction operation $C$ to attempt to correct an error $E,$ then this correction succeeds so long as the composition $CE$ is proportional to a stabilizer element.\n"
"Given that there are $2^r$ elements in the stabilizer, it follows that each correction operation $C$ corrects $2^r$ different Pauli errors.\n"
"This leaves $4^{n-r}$ inequivalent classes of Pauli operations, considered as errors, that are consistent with each possible syndrome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara lain untuk mengatakan ini adalah bahawa jika kita menggunakan operasi pembetulan $C$ untuk cuba membetulkan ralat $E,$ maka pembetulan ini berjaya selagi komposisi $CE$ adalah berkadar dengan elemen penstabil.\n"
"Memandangkan terdapat $2^r$ elemen dalam penstabil, ia mengikuti bahawa setiap operasi pembetulan $C$ membetulkan $2^r$ ralat Pauli yang berbeza.\n"
"Ini meninggalkan $4^{n-r}$ kelas tidak setara operasi Pauli, dianggap sebagai ralat, yang konsisten dengan setiap sindrom yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means that, unless $n=r$ (in which case we have a trivial, one-dimensional code space), we can't possibly correct every error detected by a stabilizer code.\n"
"What we must do instead is to choose just *one* correction operation for each syndrome, in the hopes of correcting just one class of equivalent errors that cause this syndrome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini bermakna bahawa, kecuali $n=r$ (dalam hal ini kita mempunyai ruang kod satu dimensi yang trivial), kita tidak mungkin dapat membetulkan setiap ralat yang dikesan oleh kod penstabil.\n"
"Yang perlu kita lakukan sebaliknya adalah memilih hanya *satu* operasi pembetulan untuk setiap sindrom, dengan harapan untuk membetulkan hanya satu kelas ralat setara yang menyebabkan sindrom ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One natural strategy for choosing which correction operation to perform for each syndrome is to choose the *lowest weight* Pauli operation that, as an error, causes that syndrome.\n"
"There may in fact be multiple operations that tie for the lowest weight error consistent with a given syndrome, in which case any one of them may be selected.\n"
"The idea is that lower-weight Pauli operations represent more likely explanations for whatever syndrome has been measured.\n"
"This might actually not be the case for some noise models, and one alternative strategy is to compute the most *likely* error that causes the given syndrome, based on the chosen noise model.\n"
"For this lesson, however, we'll keep things simple and only consider lowest-weight corrections.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu strategi semula jadi untuk memilih operasi pembetulan yang hendak dilakukan untuk setiap sindrom adalah memilih operasi Pauli *berat terendah* yang, sebagai ralat, menyebabkan sindrom tersebut.\n"
"Mungkin terdapat beberapa operasi yang mempunyai berat ralat terendah yang konsisten dengan sindrom tertentu, dalam hal ini mana-mana satu daripadanya boleh dipilih.\n"
"Ideanya adalah bahawa operasi Pauli berat lebih rendah mewakili penjelasan yang lebih mungkin untuk sindrom yang telah diukur.\n"
"Ini mungkin sebenarnya bukan kes untuk sesetengah model bunyi, dan satu strategi alternatif adalah mengira ralat yang paling *mungkin* menyebabkan sindrom yang diberikan, berdasarkan model bunyi yang dipilih.\n"
"Untuk pelajaran ini, bagaimanapun, kita akan memastikan perkara mudah dan hanya mempertimbangkan pembetulan berat terendah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a distance $d$ stabilizer code, this strategy of choosing the correction operation to be a lowest weight Pauli operation consistent with the measured syndrome always allows for the correction of errors having weight strictly less than half of $d,$ or in other words, weight at most $(d-1)/2.$\n"
"This shows, for instance, that the 7-qubit Steane code can correct for any weight-one Pauli error, and by the discretization of errors, this means that the Steane code can correct for an arbitrary error on one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kod penstabil jarak $d$, strategi memilih operasi pembetulan sebagai operasi Pauli berat terendah yang konsisten dengan sindrom yang diukur sentiasa membolehkan pembetulan ralat yang mempunyai berat kurang daripada separuh $d$, atau dengan kata lain, berat paling banyak $(d-1)/2.$\n"
"Ini menunjukkan, sebagai contoh, bahawa kod Steane 7-qubit boleh membetulkan sebarang ralat Pauli berat satu, dan oleh pendiskretan ralat, ini bermakna bahawa kod Steane boleh membetulkan ralat sembarangan pada satu qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see how this works, consider the diagram below.\n"
"The circle on the left represents all of the Pauli operations that result in the syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ which is the syndrome that suggests that no errors have occurred and nothing is wrong.\n"
"Among these operations we have elements of the stabilizer (or operations that are *proportional* to elements of the stabilizer, to be more precise) and we also have non-trivial errors that change the code space in some way but aren't detected by the code.\n"
"By the definition of distance, every Pauli operation in this category must have weight at least $d,$ because $d$ is defined as the minimum weight of these operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk melihat cara ini berfungsi, pertimbangkan gambar rajah di bawah.\n"
"Bulatan di sebelah kiri mewakili semua operasi Pauli yang menghasilkan sindrom $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ yang merupakan sindrom yang mencadangkan bahawa tiada ralat berlaku dan tiada yang salah.\n"
"Antara operasi ini kita mempunyai elemen penstabil (atau operasi yang *berkadar* dengan elemen penstabil, untuk lebih tepat) dan juga kita mempunyai ralat tidak trivial yang mengubah ruang kod dengan cara tertentu tetapi tidak dikesan oleh kod.\n"
"Mengikut definisi jarak, setiap operasi Pauli dalam kategori ini mestilah mempunyai berat sekurang-kurangnya $d,$ kerana $d$ ditakrifkan sebagai berat minimum operasi ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circle on the right represents the Pauli operations that result in a "
"different syndrome $s\\neq(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ including an error $E$ having "
"weight strictly less than $d/2$ that we will consider.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bulatan di sebelah kanan mewakili operasi Pauli yang menghasilkan sindrom "
"berbeza $s\\neq(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ termasuk ralat $E$ yang mempunyai berat "
"kurang daripada $d/2$ yang akan kita pertimbangkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Lowest-weight error correction "
"diagram](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/lowest-weight-correction.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Gambar rajah pembetulan ralat berat "
"terendah](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/lowest-weight-correction.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The correction operation $C$ chosen for the syndrome $s$ is the lowest weight Pauli operation in the collection represented by the circle on the right in the diagram (or any one of them in case there's a tie).\n"
"So, it could be that $C = E,$ but not necessarily.\n"
"What we can say for certain, however, is that $C$ cannot have weight larger than the weight of $E,$ because $C$ has minimal weight among the operations in this collection — and therefore $C$ has weight strictly less than $d/2.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi pembetulan $C$ yang dipilih untuk sindrom $s$ adalah operasi Pauli berat terendah dalam koleksi yang diwakili oleh bulatan di sebelah kanan dalam gambar rajah (atau mana-mana satu daripadanya jika terdapat seri).\n"
"Jadi, mungkin sahaja $C = E,$ tetapi tidak semestinya.\n"
"Apa yang boleh kita katakan dengan pasti, bagaimanapun, adalah bahawa $C$ tidak boleh mempunyai berat yang lebih besar daripada berat $E,$ kerana $C$ mempunyai berat minimum antara operasi dalam koleksi ini — dan oleh itu $C$ mempunyai berat kurang daripada $d/2.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now consider what happens when the correction operation $C$ is applied to whatever state we obtained after the error $E$ takes place.\n"
"Assuming that the original encoding was $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ we're left with $CE\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Our goal will be to show that $CE$ is proportional to an element in the stabilizer, implying that the correction is successful and (up to a global phase) we're left with the original encoded state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang pertimbangkan apa yang berlaku apabila operasi pembetulan $C$ digunakan pada apa jua keadaan yang kita perolehi selepas ralat $E$ berlaku.\n"
"Dengan mengandaikan pengekodan asal adalah $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ kita ditinggalkan dengan $CE\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Matlamat kita adalah untuk menunjukkan bahawa $CE$ adalah berkadar dengan elemen dalam penstabil, yang bermaksud pembetulan berjaya dan (sehingga fasa global) kita ditinggalkan dengan keadaan terkod asal $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, because $E$ and $C$ cause the same syndrome, the composition $CE$ must commute with every stabilizer generator.\n"
"In particular, if $P_k$ is any one of the stabilizer generators, then we must have\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kerana $E$ dan $C$ menyebabkan sindrom yang sama, komposisi $CE$ mestilah kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap penjana penstabil.\n"
"Khususnya, jika $P_k$ adalah mana-mana satu daripada penjana penstabil, maka kita mestilah ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_k E = \\alpha E P_k\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"P_k C = \\alpha C P_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_k E = \\alpha E P_k\n"
"\\quad\\text{dan}\\quad\n"
"P_k C = \\alpha C P_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for the same value of $\\alpha\\in\\{+1,-1\\},$ because this is the $k$-th entry in the syndrome $s$ that both $C$ and $E$ generate.\n"
"Hence, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk nilai $\\alpha\\in\\{+1,-1\\}$ yang sama, kerana ini adalah entri ke-$k$ dalam sindrom $s$ yang dihasilkan oleh kedua-dua $C$ dan $E$.\n"
"Oleh itu, kita ada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_k (CE) = \\alpha C P_k E = \\alpha^2 (CE) P_k = (CE) P_k,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_k (CE) = \\alpha C P_k E = \\alpha^2 (CE) P_k = (CE) P_k,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so $P_k$ commutes with $CE.$\n"
"We've therefore shown that $CE$ belongs in the circle on the left in the diagram, because it generates the syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$\n"
msgstr ""
"jadi $P_k$ kalis tukar tertib dengan $CE.$\n"
"Dengan itu kita telah menunjukkan bahawa $CE$ termasuk dalam bulatan di sebelah kiri dalam gambar rajah, kerana ia menghasilkan sindrom $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, the composition $CE$ must have weight at most the sum of the weights of $C$ and $E$ — which follows from a moment's thought about products of Pauli operations — and therefore the weight of $CE$ is strictly less than $d.$\n"
"This implies that $CE$ is proportional to an element in the stabilizer of our code, which is what we wanted to show.\n"
"By choosing our correction operations to be lowest-weight representatives of the set of errors that generate each syndrome, we're therefore guaranteed to correct any Pauli errors having weight less than half of the distance of the code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua, komposisi $CE$ mestilah mempunyai berat paling banyak hasil tambah berat $C$ dan $E$ — yang mengikuti dari sejenak berfikir tentang hasil darab operasi Pauli — dan oleh itu berat $CE$ adalah kurang daripada $d.$\n"
"Ini bermakna $CE$ adalah berkadar dengan elemen dalam penstabil kod kita, yang itulah yang kita ingin tunjukkan.\n"
"Dengan memilih operasi pembetulan kita sebagai wakil berat terendah bagi set ralat yang menghasilkan setiap sindrom, kita oleh itu dijamin untuk membetulkan sebarang ralat Pauli yang mempunyai berat kurang daripada separuh jarak kod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is one problem, however.\n"
"For stabilizer codes in general, it's a computationally difficult problem to compute the lowest weight Pauli operation causing a given syndrome.\n"
"(Indeed, this is true even for classical codes, which in this context we can think of as stabilizer codes where we only have $\\mathbb{I}$ and $Z$ matrices appearing as tensor factors within the stabilizer generators.)\n"
"So, unlike the encoding step, Clifford operations will not be coming to our rescue this time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, terdapat satu masalah.\n"
"Untuk kod penstabil secara umum, ia adalah masalah yang sukar secara pengiraan untuk mengira operasi Pauli berat terendah yang menyebabkan sindrom tertentu.\n"
"(Malah, ini benar walaupun untuk kod klasik, yang dalam konteks ini boleh kita fikirkan sebagai kod penstabil di mana hanya matriks $\\mathbb{I}$ dan $Z$ muncul sebagai faktor tensor dalam penjana penstabil.)\n"
"Jadi, tidak seperti langkah pengekodan, operasi Clifford tidak akan datang menyelamatkan kita kali ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The solution is to choose specific codes for which good corrections can be computed efficiently, for which there's no simple recipe.\n"
"Simply put, devising stabilizer codes for which good correction operations can be computed efficiently is part of the artistry of quantum code design.\n"
"We'll see this artistry on display in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penyelesaiannya adalah memilih kod khusus yang pembetulan baik boleh dikira dengan cekap, yang tiada resipi mudah untuk itu.\n"
"Secara ringkasnya, mereka bentuk kod penstabil yang operasi pembetulan baik boleh dikira dengan cekap adalah sebahagian daripada kesenian reka bentuk kod kuantum.\n"
"Kita akan melihat kesenian ini dipamerkan dalam pelajaran seterusnya.\n"
